@*
    The one rule that keeps a press on a link out of the prose that holds it.

    The description of a bead is press to edit: a press on the prose opens its
    box. The prose is rendered markdown, so it carries links of its own, and a
    press on one of those means the page it names and not the box. The browser
    is where the pressed element is known, so the rule lives here, in the
    capture phase, before the press reaches the prose.
*@

<script>
    document.addEventListener("click", function (press) {
        var link = press.target.closest("a");
        if (link !== null && link.closest(".bead-prose-pressable") !== null) {
            press.stopPropagation();
        }
    }, true);
</script>
